Provenance notice
=================

This project is a personal, educational reconstruction of the video-only
watermark-removal feature of the locally installed Chrome extension:

  Erasio - Automate Google Flow, Gemini and Google Vids
  Extension ID: aedhekmakfgbcknofpiccffacdjcgdpp
  Version: 1.3.1

Files copied verbatim from that local installation:

  vendor/videoProcessor.js       <- page/videoProcessor.js
                                 (plus 3 added lines exporting
                                  __decodeVideoFrames / __erasioInpaintFrame for the
                                  standalone preview path)
  vendor/sparkleEngine.js        <- page/sparkleEngine.js   (byte-identical, SHA-256 checked)
  vendor/veoTextEngine.js        <- page/veoTextEngine.js
  vendor/veoTextTemplates.js     <- page/veoTextTemplates.js
  vendor/watermarkEngine.js      <- page/watermarkEngine.js   (kept, not loaded)
  vendor/mp4box.all.min.js       <- page/vendor/mp4box.all.min.js
  vendor/mp4-muxer.min.js        <- page/vendor/mp4-muxer.min.js
  masks/bg_48.png                <- assets/bg_48.png
  masks/bg_96.png                <- assets/bg_96.png
  masks/gemini-star_paired_star_mask.png <- assets/gemini-star_paired_star_mask.png
  masks/sparkle-2026-48.png      <- assets/sparkle-2026-48.png
  masks/sparkle-2026-96.png      <- assets/sparkle-2026-96.png

The video constants reproduced in js/detect.js (offset tables [144,120,128,72] and
[222,186], opacity levels [1,0.62], the mask table, the Pearson position score,
the two-level opacity estimate and the edge-cleanup rule) were read out of the
extension's side-panel bundle, which is not redistributed here.

The Veo templates are marked GENERATED in their header and were copied byte-for-byte
from the MIT-licensed gemini-watermark-remover runtime that the extension itself vendors:
  - https://github.com/GargantuaX/gemini-watermark-remover

The reconstructed pipeline follows the algorithm described in the source
comments of videoProcessor.js:

  "Port of geminiwatermarkremove.net's algorithm ..."
  "Based on GeminiWatermarkTool by Allen Kuo (allenk)."
  - https://github.com/allenk/geminiwatermarktool

Third-party libraries bundled in vendor/:
  - MP4Box.js        (mp4box.all.min.js, header: "mp4box 19-03-2022")
  - mp4-muxer 5.2.1  (mp4-muxer.min.js, jsDelivr/Terser build)

The UI (index.html, styles.css, js/app.js), README and repository scaffolding
are original to this project.

No affiliation with Erasio, Google, or the authors of the upstream components
is implied. Review the upstream licences before redistributing.
